3. Sharing mods and patches

You may distribute mods without charge as original add-on code, original
data, original assets or patches that require a separately obtained lawful
copy of Orion Reach. A patch may include the limited project source context
needed to identify and apply its changes. This permission does not authorize
redistributing the complete game, complete replacement copies of existing
game source files, or extracted game artwork or music.

Retain relevant notices, include this license when a patch contains project
material, identify the supported game version, and clearly identify the mod
as unofficial and its changes as yours. Only include material you may lawfully
share. You retain any rights in your own contributions; this license does
not assign those rights to the Licensor. Receiving a mod grants no additional
rights to the underlying game. Paid mods require separate written permission.

See docs/modding-policy.md for practical examples of these rules.

